# Root-level pointer (docs/07-devops.md §1's repo layout — this file lives
# here even though both subprojects also ship their own, narrower
# `.env.example`, per CLAUDE.md's Commands table listing root-level `make`
# targets). Copy each subproject's file to its real name before `make up`:
#
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env.local
#
# Backend variables (repository backend, database URL, tenant, AWS/Anthropic
# credentials for the S3/Anthropic adapters) are documented in
# backend/.env.example — never duplicated here, so there is one place each
# variable's default and meaning are defined.
#
# Frontend variables (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, mock latency) are documented
# in frontend/.env.example.
#
# Nothing in this repo reads a root-level `.env` file directly — `Settings`
# (backend/src/openspec/config/settings.py) reads `backend/.env`; Next.js
# reads `frontend/.env.local`. This file exists so the two are discoverable
# from one place, matching the documented repo layout, not to be loaded
# itself.
